Wed May 17 20:38:03 MDT 2006
Dataman 3.3.0
server -
	Finally got a 64 bit machine to compile on, and found various type
	problems.  This will now run a 64 bit database on both 32 bit and
	64 bit CPUs (using gcc).  Changed the threading so that at system
	startup worker threads are spun up, and not a new one for each
	command received.  Removed some un-necessary memcpy's.  All in all
	these changes improve performance ~12%.  Fixed a long standing bug
	in delete().  Added a command line argument to set the number of
	worker threads, and one to set the size of the shared memory area
	used for thread communication with connections. The defaults for
	these are 10 threads and 1K shared mem segments.
client -
	Had to change some of the variables for 64 bit CPUs.  Delete bug
	was here too.
overall -
	rolled up the new release 3.3.0

Tue Jan 17 21:08:49 MST 2006
server -
	Changed up file locking a little again, should be a -little- more
	efficient.  Also in all of the get routines and restore if you had to
	call rm_key there would be a deadlock.

Dataman 3.2.5
Wed Dec 28 20:55:12 MST 2005
server -
	Changed both user level and system level locking.  The original dataman
	used to write a bit to the record header when performing a protect call.
	Now, the server will keep a list of protected records, so if there is a
	server crash, the records won't remain protected.  System level locking
	now implements the idea of lock owners.  If you didn't assert a lock,
	you can't remove one.  Also, there could have been resource starvation
	if there was a thread waiting to assert a write lock, and read locks
	continued to occur.  A queue is now implemented for this case.
overall -
	rolled up all of the changes into a new release 3.2.5

Tue Dec 27 21:10:14 MST 2005
server and client -
	Went through the server and client routines and ran lint over most of
	them.  Trying to clean up some crufty stuff.

Mon Dec 26 16:57:03 MST 2005
server - 
	Two ugly bugs.  I can't believe these didn't get caught.  Two apps
	using the same work file (init_dataman) and identical index (iopen)
	would fail.  Would not let you run two instances of the same
	application.

Sat Nov 19 17:04:02 MST 2005
client -
	pre-set dm_sock to be -1.  This lets php start and stop with no
	dataman calls at all terminate without an attempt to disconnect
	from the server.  Otherwise you get a stupid error message.

Tue Nov  8 17:04:02 MST 2005
